      "worked": "When $x=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(2)&=(2-3)^2\\\\f(2)&=1\\\\f_L(2)&=a\\\\f_R(2)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nContinuity requires all three values to agree, so $a=1$.\n\nWhen $x=6$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(6)&=(6-3)^2\\\\f(6)&=9\\\\f_L(6)&=9\\\\f_R(6)&=b-6\\end{align*}$$\nContinuity requires\n$$\\begin{align*}b-6&=9\\\\b&=15\\end{align*}$$\nEach branch is continuous on its interval. With $a=1$ and $b=15$, the values also agree at both boundaries, so $f$ is continuous throughout its domain.",
